Z||000006||88formula||01-23-2000||09:37 PM||||DRH, I tried the fix and it worked OK. Thanks, you saved me time and $90. Now I just have to devise a way to make a water shield so that water does not get back in.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||01-23-2000||09:43 PM||||I'm surprised this is such a common problem. Mine wasn't frozen this morning, I'm sure it will be tommorrow as it isn't in the garage this time. I've read the page on the link several times, but I'm just not able to follow it all the way through. Something about a vaccume cleaner and wd-40?||||reg||1
Z||000008||baggy||01-25-2000||12:33 AM||||my lil red bandit runs better when it gets cold..<BR>i havent had the first wire get hot and melt since it finally turned cold..<BR>ALL HAIL!!<BR>FATHER WINTER!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||01-25-2000||08:40 AM||||he's using the vac on one end of the cable to draw the oil into the other. Probably a little easier to set up than a pressure feed, but doesn't remove as much dirt.||||reg||1
